Qore PDFium dependency for Ubuntu 26.04
=====================================

The PDFium commit and every dependency commit are recorded in
QORE-SOURCE-MANIFEST.json. The source archive contains no downloaded SDK,
compiler or prebuilt library. GN is bootstrapped from its pinned source,
with the upstream commit position recorded explicitly for reproducibility.
Builds require no network access. The source archive excludes unused
Android binaries, test fixtures/fonts and macOS APSL allocator files.

The private C++ dependency closure is linked into one DSO; only FPDF*,
FORM_* and FSDK_* public C symbols are exported. System ICU, FreeType,
LCMS, OpenJPEG, JPEG, PNG, TIFF, zlib and Brotli are used. No V8, XFA or
Skia dependency is needed by Qore's rendering and text extraction APIs.
The SONAME includes milestone 148 because PDFium does not promise ABI
compatibility between milestones. The development package has an exact
runtime dependency and a distinct include directory and pkg-config name.

The original Qore CI pin is Chromium branch 7778, commit
72ea487e4399c44c3a53a48b104f9612ca772008. Future security updates must be
reviewed against this upstream branch; a new milestone requires a new
SONAME and rebuild of the Qore PDF module. This testing package does not
establish a security maintenance policy for a general release.

Build with dpkg-buildpackage -b -us -uc. Debian build flags apply to the
library; native amd64 and arm64 toolchain mappings are provided. Cross
compilation is rejected. Only architectures actually tested should be
published. The build and autopkgtest exercise the public C API, including
real rendered pixels and text extraction. They do not claim to replace
the complete upstream PDFium test suite.

Split DWARF is disabled so the automatic dbgsym package contains complete
debug information rather than references to build-directory .dwo files.
